  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 1,
   "text": "Topic 3: Properties of expectation and variance",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "4066bbd0-7496-51dc-af43-67dd393961cc"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "These rules turn most \"find $E$ / Var of something\" questions into one line.",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "bd71e3ae-1e43-58c6-97ac-1e95970a1718"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "E[aX+b]=a\\,E[X]+b\\qquad E[aX+bY]=a\\,E[X]+b\\,E[Y]",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "b8fcca89-f00b-4b0a-8a73-1aec471f4407",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "0eb0a16e-6d2c-40a6-83e1-031a1f0dae55"
    }
   ],
   "id": "d32ed5d4-55f3-5536-a459-33b855043863"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "\\operatorname{Var}(aX+b)=a^2\\operatorname{Var}(X)\\qquad \\sigma_{aX+b}=|a|\\,\\sigma_X",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "b8fcca89-f00b-4b0a-8a73-1aec471f4407",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "35a0186d-c0e5-48d4-89d2-9f5548bcda6b"
    }
   ],
   "id": "a7a82878-46a5-52d5-a2e8-0f415e8b6113"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "items": [
    "**Shifting** by $b$ moves the centre but **not** the spread: $b$ disappears from Var.",
    "**Scaling** by $a$ scales the spread by $|a|$, so Var by $a^2$. A minus sign never makes Var negative: $\\operatorname{Var}(-X)=\\operatorname{Var}(X)$.",
    "$E[b]=b$ and $\\operatorname{Var}(b)=0$ for a constant $b$.",
    "**Turn the shortcut around:** $E[X^2]=\\operatorname{Var}(X)+(E[X])^2$. Use it whenever you are given $E$ and Var."
   ],
   "ordered": false,
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "52e9fc11-81ed-4bab-a495-7e4b29f79a8b",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "72ec1f08-5a0f-478f-8963-c20f6396f281"
    }
   ],
   "id": "cac32a8b-aba1-568a-bb21-dd08f14a5ac2"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "```steps\ntitle \"Why $\\operatorname{Var}(aX+b)=a^2\\operatorname{Var}(X)$\"\n$$\n\\operatorname{Var}(aX+b)=E\\big[(aX+b-E[aX+b])^2\\big]\n$$\nDefinition, with $Y=aX+b$.\n$$\n=E\\big[(aX+b-\\hl{aE[X]-b})^2\\big]\n$$\nLinearity of $E$.\n$$\n=E\\big[\\hl{a^2}(X-E[X])^2\\big]\n$$\nThe $b$ cancels; pull out $a$ and square it.\n$$\n=\\hl{a^2\\operatorname{Var}(X)}\n$$\n$a^2$ is a constant, so it comes out of $E$.\n```",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "4f9003e4-0fc9-5400-baab-d0186b8ff8f8"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "**Moments:** $E[X^n]$ is the $n$th (raw) **moment**; $E[(X-\\mu_X)^n]$ is the $n$th **central moment**. So $E[X]$ = 1st moment, $E[X^2]$ = 2nd moment, and Var = 2nd central moment.",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "52e9fc11-81ed-4bab-a495-7e4b29f79a8b",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "061ca83b-a397-4cdf-b0d0-e3f23afbc005"
    }
   ],
   "id": "5ef17055-5501-515e-a0cb-1ef1ab3fe773"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "**Means and variances to memorise** (no formula sheet). Each can be found with Topics 1–2:",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "4dffa483-d1ff-5193-95a0-a467a55c7bda"
  },
  {
