  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 3 · Sensor calibration",
   "prompt": "A sensor output $X$ has $E[X]=3$ and $\\operatorname{Var}(X)=9$. (a) Find the mean squared error $E[(2-X)^2]$. (b) The reading is calibrated as $Y=2X-3$. Find $\\operatorname{Var}(Y)$.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "(a) **Expand**, then use linearity.",
     "latex": "E[(2-X)^2]=E[4-4X+X^2]=4-4E[X]+E[X^2]"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Turn the shortcut around** to get $E[X^2]$.",
     "latex": "E[X^2]=\\operatorname{Var}(X)+(E[X])^2=9+9=18"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "Substitute.",
     "latex": "E[(2-X)^2]=4-12+18=10"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(b) **Shift drops out, scale squares.**",
     "latex": "\\operatorname{Var}(2X-3)=2^2\\cdot9=36"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "(a) $10$ (b) $36$",
   "citations": [
