  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Question 1 · A PMF table with an unknown",
   "difficulty": "introductory",
   "origin": "original",
   "prompt": "$X$ has the PMF below.\n\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| $p_X(x)$ | $0.1$ | $c$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ |\n\nFind (a) $c$, (b) $E[X]$ and $\\operatorname{Var}(X)$, (c) $E[5-2X]$ and $\\operatorname{Var}(5-2X)$.",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "(a) **Total = 1.**",
     "latex": "0.1+c+0.3+0.2=1\\;\\Rightarrow\\;c=0.4"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(b) **Mean.**",
     "latex": "E[X]=-0.1+0+0.3+0.4=0.6"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Second moment.**",
     "latex": "E[X^2]=0.1+0+0.3+0.8=1.2"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Subtract.**",
     "latex": "\\operatorname{Var}(X)=1.2-0.36=0.84"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(c) **Linearity**, then **scale squares** (the minus sign disappears).",
     "latex": "E[5-2X]=5-1.2=3.8,\\quad \\operatorname{Var}(5-2X)=4(0.84)=3.36"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$c=0.4$; $E[X]=0.6$, $\\operatorname{Var}(X)=0.84$; $E[5-2X]=3.8$, $\\operatorname{Var}(5-2X)=3.36$.",
   "citations": [],
