   "title": "Question 6 · A sensor that saturates",
   "difficulty": "intermediate",
   "origin": "original",
   "prompt": "A sensor reading $X$ saturates: with probability $0.3$ it reads exactly $X=5$; otherwise (probability $0.7$) it is uniform on $(0,5)$, so the continuous part has density $0.7\\cdot\\tfrac15=0.14$ on $(0,5)$. Find $E[X]$ and $\\operatorname{Var}(X)$.",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Mean:** point mass + integral.",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}E[X]=5(0.3)+\\int_0^5x(0.14)\\,dx\\\\ =1.5+0.14\\cdot\\frac{25}{2}=1.5+1.75=3.25\\end{gathered}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Second moment:** same split, with $x^2$.",
     "latex": "E[X^2]=25(0.3)+\\int_0^5x^2(0.14)\\,dx=7.5+0.14\\cdot\\frac{125}{3}=\\frac{40}{3}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Subtract.**",
     "latex": "\\operatorname{Var}(X)=\\frac{40}{3}-3.25^2=\\frac{133}{48}\\approx2.771"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$E[X]=3.25$, $\\operatorname{Var}(X)=\\tfrac{133}{48}\\approx2.771$.",
