   "difficulty": "intermediate",
   "origin": "source",
   "prompt": "A rover returns 560 g of material in four canisters A, B, C, D holding $140$, $112$, $125$ and $183$ g. First a **canister** is chosen at random (each $\\tfrac14$); $x$ = grams in it. Then a **1-gram sample** is chosen at random from all 560 g; $y$ = grams in the canister it came from. (a) Which of $E[x]$, $E[y]$ should be larger, and why? (b) Compute both.",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "(a) For $y$, a canister is picked with probability **proportional to its mass**, so heavy canisters count more. Expect $E[y]>E[x]$.",
     "latex": "P(y=m)=\\frac{m}{560}"
    },
