   "difficulty": "intermediate",
   "origin": "original",
   "prompt": "$X$ has the triangular PDF $f_X(x)=x$ on $[0,1]$, $f_X(x)=2-x$ on $[1,2]$, and $0$ otherwise. Find $E[X]$, $\\operatorname{Var}(X)$, and $\\operatorname{Var}(2X+3)$.",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Mean:** the triangle is symmetric about $x=1$.",
     "latex": "E[X]=1"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Second moment:** split the integral at $x=1$.",
     "latex": "E[X^2]=\\int_0^1x^3\\,dx+\\int_1^2x^2(2-x)\\,dx"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "Integrate each piece.",
     "latex": "=\\frac14+\\left[\\frac{2x^3}{3}-\\frac{x^4}{4}\\right]_1^2=\\frac14+\\frac{11}{12}=\\frac76"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Subtract.**",
     "latex": "\\operatorname{Var}(X)=\\frac76-1=\\frac16"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Scale squares.**",
     "latex": "\\operatorname{Var}(2X+3)=4\\cdot\\frac16=\\frac23"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$E[X]=1$, $\\operatorname{Var}(X)=\\tfrac16$, $\\operatorname{Var}(2X+3)=\\tfrac23$.",
