   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Question 10 · Find the constants, then the variance · Tutorial 6 Q6",
   "difficulty": "advanced",
   "origin": "source",
   "prompt": "$X$ has PDF\n\n$$\nf_X(x)=\\frac{C}{1+(x+K)^2},\\qquad -K-1\\le x\\le -K+1,\n$$\n\nand $0$ otherwise, where $C>0$ and $K$ are constants. (a) Find $C$ and $K$ so that $E[X]=5$. (b) Find $\\operatorname{Var}(X)$.",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Shift:** let $u=x+K$, so $u\\in[-1,1]$ and $X=U-K$ with $f_U(u)=\\frac{C}{1+u^2}$.",
     "latex": "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\frac{C}{1+u^2}\\,du=C\\big[\\arctan u\\big]_{-1}^{1}=C\\cdot\\frac{\\pi}{2}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(a) **Total area = 1.**",
     "latex": "C=\\frac{2}{\\pi}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "$f_U$ is **even**, so $E[U]=0$. Then use linearity.",
     "latex": "E[X]=E[U]-K=-K=5\\;\\Rightarrow\\;K=-5"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(b) A shift does not change Var, and $E[U]=0$.",
     "latex": "\\operatorname{Var}(X)=\\operatorname{Var}(U)=E[U^2]"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "Write $\\frac{u^2}{1+u^2}=1-\\frac{1}{1+u^2}$.",
     "latex": "E[U^2]=\\frac2\\pi\\int_{-1}^{1}\\Big(1-\\frac{1}{1+u^2}\\Big)du=\\frac2\\pi\\Big(2-\\frac\\pi2\\Big)"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "Simplify.",
     "latex": "\\operatorname{Var}(X)=\\frac4\\pi-1\\approx0.2732"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "(a) $C=\\tfrac2\\pi$, $K=-5$ (so $X\\in[4,6]$) (b) $\\operatorname{Var}(X)=\\tfrac4\\pi-1\\approx0.2732$",
